[{"result":{"data":{"json":{"id":"411","stub":{"id":"411","section":"03. Lower Piedra CG to Navajo Reservoir","altname":"","river":"Piedra","difficulty":"IItoIII","states":["USA-COL"]},"primaryGaugeStatus":{"status":"below-recommended","latestReading":{"value":"309","dateTime":"2026-05-12T02:15:00.000Z","qualifier":"NORMAL"},"metric":"cfs","adjustedDifficulty":null},"pointOfInterests":[{"type":"put-in","description":null,"id":"107791","location":{"latitude":"37.2406","longitude":"-107.342"},"name":"Put In","distance":"0","photoID":null,"difficulty":"N/A","approximate":false},{"type":"takeout","description":null,"id":"113033","location":{"latitude":"37.0628","longitude":"-107.414"},"name":"Take Out","distance":"18.2","photoID":null,"difficulty":"N/A","approximate":false}],"alerts":[{"id":"101253593","title":null,"post_date":"2018-05-20 04:00:00+00","detail":"Significant hazard on this lower Piedra run. I came across 2 strands of barbed wire, one mostly submerged and the other at chest level for a kayaker. I almost didn't see the first one as I was looking at some very cool rock formations on the left and looked up just before I drifted into it. You'll know you're close if you look on a map to find where Fosset Rd. comes down to the river and a ranch right there.","user":{"name":"Dana Hays"}}],"photos":[{"id":"z90zbJgmyXQpxsWgg22hX","ext":"jpg","post_id":"Rwc93pAekJLQoHjUd7Itq","description":"<p>One of many many diversion dams on the stretch. We ran it a little below recommended flows, so they were bony. There are around 25-30 of these on the stretch, some with one drop, some with 2</p>","caption":"Diversion Dam below put-in","poi_name":null,"subject":"Beta","author":"Peter Bradley","poi_id":"107791","photo_date":"2025-06-12T04:22:54.000Z","updated_at":"2025-06-12T04:22:54.000Z","url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/z90zbJgmyXQpxsWgg22hX","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/z90zbJgmyXQpxsWgg22hX"}},{"id":"885198","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"887899","description":"Lower Piedra at ~850cfs","caption":"5/9/15 ~850cfs","poi_name":null,"subject":null,"author":"cupcake","poi_id":null,"photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/885198","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/885198"}}],"detail":{"id":"411","permitUrl":"","permitInfo":"","description":"**IMPORTANT:** Please visit the [Southern Ute Indian Tribe's website](https://www.southernute-nsn.gov/natural-resources/wildlife-resource-management/fishing/stream-fishing-regulations/#streamAccess) for regulations on boating and fishing the Piedra River within the SUIT reservation boundaries. The Tribe permits non-Tribal members to float through reservation lands on the Animas River, Los Pinos River, the Piedra River, and the San Juan River. **However**, only people who are actively fishing (and with a valid fishing permit) using a small craft may put-in or take-out at specified fishing access points. See below for additional information should you choose to complete the entire 18 mile run in one day.\n\nWithin a mile of the Piedra Campground, the river canyon starts opening up. The valley gets wider and the river meanders more the further it goes. Most of the rapids are in the first few miles, but it looks like there can be waves and riffles here and there most of the way to the reservoir and even into the reservoir when it is low.\n\n**Getting There:** This section of the Piedra is just north of the Colorado- New Mexico border and is about 50 minutes east of Durango Colorado.\n\nThe put in elevation is about 6590 feet and the take out is about 6096 feet, for a total drop of 494 feet over 18 miles.\n\n**Other Information Sources**:\n\n[San Juan National Forest](http://www.fs.usda.gov/sanjuan/)\n\n[Navajo State Park](http://cpw.state.co.us/placestogo/parks/Navajo)","averageGradient":"27","maxGradient":"53","length":"17.6","correlations":[{"reachID":"411","isPrimary":true,"correlationDetails":{"metric":"cfs","belowRecommendedRangeComment":null,"lowRunnableRangeComment":null,"mediumRunnableRangeComment":null,"highRunnableRangeComment":null,"aboveRecommendedRangeComment":null,"lowRunnableAdjustedDifficulty":null,"highRunnableAdjustedDifficulty":null,"beginLowRunnable":"400","beginMediumRunnable":null,"beginHighRunnable":null,"endHighRunnable":"4000"},"gaugeInfo":{"name":"PIEDRA RIVER NEAR ARBOLES, CO.","gaugeSource":"USGS","gaugeSourceIdentifier":"09349800","gaugeFetchStatus":"ACTIVE","latestFlowReading":{"value":"309","dateTime":"2026-05-12T02:15:00.000Z","qualifier":"NORMAL"},"latestStageReading":{"value":"1.18","dateTime":"2026-05-12T02:15:00.000Z","qualifier":"NORMAL"},"location":{"latitude":"37.08834204","longitude":"-107.3978428"},"externalSourceLinks":{"sourceLink":{"url":"https://water.noaa.gov/gauges/09349800","text":"NOAA"},"secondaryLink":{"url":"https://waterdata.usgs.gov/monitoring-location/09349800/#parameterCode=00060&period=P7D","text":"US Geological Survey"}}},"migrationErrorExplanation":"Previous Flowbands: \nRange of Boatable Flows (R0-R9): 400 - 4000 cfs  Comment: Guesstimate of  boatable range\n\nMigration Errors: \nSingle range is valid but doesn't provide low/medium/high runnable\nThere is one comment for all of low/medium/high runnable.","comment":null,"status":{"status":"below-recommended","latestReading":{"value":"309","dateTime":"2026-05-12T02:15:00.000Z","qualifier":"NORMAL"},"metric":"cfs","adjustedDifficulty":null}}],"pointOfInterestIDs":["107791","113033"],"geometry":{"type":"LineString","coordinates":[[-107.34193233,37.2405867],[-107.34231148,37.23865708],[-107.34226968,37.23696728],[-107.34226421,37.23610528],[-107.34239221,37.23546028],[-107.34278108,37.23504681],[-107.34329788,37.23466468],[-107.34348441,37.23454268],[-107.34358941,37.23458368],[-107.34357121,37.23427648],[-107.34358121,37.23400068],[-107.34367828,37.23389721],[-107.34353328,37.23365908],[-107.34315221,37.23248228